  "details": "A way for users to tag avatars they upload and hide avatars with those tags\n\nAn example of those tags | Screen effects, flashing lights, loud audio, Gore, violence, Explicit, NSFW, repetitive audio\nthese would be similar to the CVR tags.\n\nIn a users safety settings people can chose to show or hide these tags, this could be done with a \"fold down\" section of the safety menu in each trust level, this would mean that people can chose to block avatars that contain these effects for certain trust levels\n\nA way to implement NSFW filtering, add a DLC or a verification page on the website (just inputting age / DOB ) without this verification explicit and NSFW avatars would always be hidden, of course there will still be underage people that get past this but this should remove any liability that VRChat has \n\nThese tags could also help people with epilepsy or Tourette's, this would allow these users to filter out avatars that may have objects that trigger seizures or tics such as flashing lights, screen effects and certain types of audio",
